{#- State template of the UI helper "Grundpreis je Stunde" (Template → Sensor,
    sensor.electricity_base_rate, unit EUR/h, state class measurement, not
    exposed to Assist). The monthly base price of the active tariff slot (see
    electricity_work_price.jinja) spread over the hours of the current
    calendar month. The Integral helper "Grundpreis" (sensor.electricity_base_cost,
    left Riemann sum, time unit hours, max sub-interval 15 min) adds it up in
    EUR, so the recorder keeps the base price as a statistic next to the
    energy cost. Months are counted as whole days: in the months with the DST
    change the result is off by one hour in 743 or 745 (0.13 %). -#}
{%- set ns = namespace(start='', value=none) -%}
{%- set today = now().date() | string -%}
{%- for i in range(1, 4) -%}
  {%- set start = states('input_datetime.electricity_tariff_' ~ i ~ '_valid_from') -%}
  {%- set work = states('input_number.electricity_tariff_' ~ i ~ '_work_price') | float(0) -%}
  {%- if work > 0 and start is match('[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$') and start <= today and start > ns.start -%}
    {%- set ns.start = start -%}
    {%- set ns.value = states('input_number.electricity_tariff_' ~ i ~ '_base_price') | float(0) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set first = now().replace(day=1, hour=0, minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0) -%}
{%- set hours = (((first + timedelta(days=32)).replace(day=1) - first).days * 24) -%}
{{ (ns.value / hours) | round(6) if ns.value is not none else none }}
